            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Amanda Zobava"
            },
            "reviewBody": "No. This recipe is backwards. By the time the Brussel sprouts are done the onion is burned to a crisp. Brussel sprouts should be cooked first until almost done then add onion for about 5 minutes and then garlic for last 2 minutes.",
            "datePublished": "2018-11-03T00:53:45.117Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Betty Larrison"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I did olive oil generous amount, I then cut the brussels sprouts the stem came off if were to big I cut in half fried in pan, maybe 20 mins added onions garlic and TBS of bacon grease then I put a lid on it cooked till my desire salt and pepper , they were delicious and will be making again hope this helps",
            "datePublished": "2025-01-10T22:01:22.578Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "janmauss"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Super simple, fast, and delicious. Comments include some good ideas, but this one is perfect for me. I prefer it to recipes that included shredded sprouts as we enjoy the mouth feel of a more identifiable sprout. I did use a lid as suggested by another commentor to steam the sprouts to be more tender and the 2nd time, used some shredded Parm as a garnish.",
            "datePublished": "2025-12-16T16:09:58.893Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
