            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Angel Lotus Song"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Very tasty! I added the garlic and onion at the same time as my Brussel sprouts and my onions still ended up a bit burnt but I still liked it. Also added some white cooking wine to the mix and steamed them a bit. I also cut them into quarters so they would cook faster.",
            "datePublished": "2018-01-05T06:13:52.240Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Andrew Fuller"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I omit the onion, use a large paella pan so I can get every cut side touching the surface for maximum roastiness, and add crushed red pepper and a drizzle of truffle oil at the finish. Not at all undelicious.",
            "datePublished": "2016-01-20T19:12:12.600Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "5"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "jenonymous"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Really good! I liked doing these on the cooktop, because my oven was busy with Chicken Parmesan Bake (Chef John!), and I needed to use the Brussels Sprouts before I had to throw them away. I did them in cast iron, and I put the garlic in at the same time as the sprouts so I didn't burn it. I used the trick with the water and the lid because the onions were burning and the sprouts weren't cooking very fast, and that evened things out nicely! My daughter's boyfriend had never had them before, and said they were delicious. I thought so too!",
            "datePublished": "2014-01-15T16:22:30.027Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "3"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "LoyalBroth4594"
            },
            "reviewBody": "As others have mentioned the sprouts aren't tender if you follow this recipe exactly. I had an instinct, and it was confirmed when I compared another recipe which advised after pan-frying a bit--cover/with a low flame for approx. 15 minutes",
            "datePublished": "2023-04-05T02:03:49.037Z"
          },
